ives to the output data types it finds. Then add a few simple fixes found with the improved diagnostic view.\r\n\r\nExample command to get the dot format graphviz:\r\n``` \r\nRUST_LOG=\"sqlx::explain=trace\" DATABASE_URL=sqlite://tests/sqlite/sqlite.db cargo test --features sqlite,runtime-tokio,tls-rustls,chrono -- --nocapture update\r\n```\r\nThen the graphviz markup can be copy-pasted into the graphviz renderer/editor of choice. The process isn't elegant, but it works.\r\n\r\n**Warning**: this only actually works when running a program which directly uses the 'describe' operation (such as sqlx's sqlite unit tests). Logger output is not available when compiling a library USING sqlx (the output is ignored - probably by rustc itself?).\r\n\r\n### Does your PR solve an issue?\r\nFixes test cases derived from #2939 & #1923  (which involves breaking changes)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/launchbadge/sqlx/issues/3064/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/launchbadge/sqlx/issues/3064/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":12546487464,"node_id":"REFE_lADODb6dM8554-cezwAAAALr1DSo","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/launchbadge/sqlx/issues/events/12546487464","actor":{"login":"tyrelr","id":44035897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDM1ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44035897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrelr","html_url":"https://github.com/tyrelr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrelr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrelr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrelr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrelr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrelr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com